We also need helmets and helmet locks on all scooters for Australia. I just got this from our public policy colleague:

{quote}I received confirmation that helmets in Australia are compulsory for all users. Cities expect operators to provide them on the vehicle.

*Helmets* - _sharing operators have to have a helmet on each vehicle (I highly doubt a city would provide a permit without this functionality). For about 3 years they have been clipped to all shared vehicles and generally required to unclip to start the trip. The way operators get around this if the helmet has been lost is by asking if the rider has their own helmet. I would say this capability (helmet clipped to vehicle and required to start trip) is a non-negotiable in the Australian market - the requirement to ride a bike with a helmet has been the case for a number of decades...A helmet is required for both e-bikes and e-scooters and it is illegal not to wear one whilst riding. It is loosely enforced._{quote}

