During this [PR|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/73314] hypotheses were checked that the query need some time limitation, for TiDB to correctly select nodes on wich to send particular query. have more limits on query by date, speeding up the processing

After it, [2d|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/73398] and [3rd|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/73472] PR were made, which significanlty improve the situation with particular queries



The outcome, for queries like

{noformat}        return this.db.findBy(
            ctx,
            TableId.orderVehicleEvent,
            this.FIELDS.toString(),
            {
                processing_state: processingState
            },{noformat}

better specify time frames like this

{noformat}{
                created: {
                    binary_op: ">",
                    value: `FROM_UNIXTIME(${TimestampHelper.nowSec() - 3600})`
                }
            },{noformat}

, for TiDB to not process whole server (even if {{processing_state}} doese have index)

same with such queries

{noformat}        const query = sql`
            SELECT ${this.FIELDS_FOR_PROCESSING}
            FROM ${TableId.orderEvent} as e
            JOIN ${TableId.order} as o ON (e.order_id = o.id)
            LEFT JOIN ${TableId.orderPartnerTrip} as opt ON (opt.order_id = o.id)
            LEFT JOIN ${TableId.paymentOrder} as po ON (po.id = e.payment_order_id)
            WHERE e.queue_sync_state = ${OrderEventState.WAITING}
            ORDER BY e.created
            LIMIT ${limit}`;{noformat}

this will execute on TiDB slower then this one

{noformat}        const query = sql`
            SELECT ${this.FIELDS_FOR_PROCESSING}
            FROM ${TableId.orderEvent} as e
            JOIN ${TableId.order} as o ON (e.order_id = o.id)
            LEFT JOIN ${TableId.orderPartnerTrip} as opt ON (opt.order_id = o.id)
            LEFT JOIN ${TableId.paymentOrder} as po ON (po.id = e.payment_order_id)
            WHERE
                e.publish_at <= FROM_UNIXTIME(${TimestampHelper.nowSec()}) AND
                e.publish_at > FROM_UNIXTIME(${TimestampHelper.nowSec() - 3600})
            LIMIT ${limit}`;{noformat}

