# Please kindly provide some background as to why do we need this agreement.

{color:#bf2600}We need to import used scooters into Turkey for operation. Turkey’s government forbids anyone from importing used goods into the country. We have found a supplier Cycletron to help us refurbish the scooters in the Aegean Free Zone and then import them into Turkey. The Turkish local authority needs us to sign a contract with Cycletron to prove distributorship so that Cycletron has the right to import the scooters under our brand.{color}

# Did we select the supplier?

{color:#bf2600}Yes, the supplier is found and selected by us{color}

# Do we need this agreement for e-bikes only or e-scooters as well?

{color:#bf2600}Currently, we are only trying to import scooters.{color}

# Can you please provide more information on Article 3? There is reference to shipping from various locations etc. Under which rule do we fall? Do you know what are they trying to say in clause 2 of Article 3 when they mention preparation of various documentation (like "preparation of user manual")?

{color:#bf2600}The plan is that we ship components of used scooters to Aegean Free zone under our costs. Cycletron will refurbish the scooters under our guidance inside the free zone. After refurbishment, Cycletron will import the scooters to a Turkish company Flex. Flex is a brother company of Cycletron. After importing the scooters, Flex will sell the scooters to Bolt Turkey.{color}

{color:#bf2600}They are right that it is our responsibility to provide the documents. We have already forwarded them the CE certificates. We are working on the user manual {color}

# How much room for negotiating terms of the agreement we have? For example, there is no termination for convenience provisions, we would like to have them.

{color:#bf2600}Apart from the distributorship clause, which is required by the local authorities, we should negotiate everything in the contract in our favour. We have leverage over this supplier {color}

# For how long should we conclude this agreement from operational perspective?

{color:#bf2600}Now everything is under testing, we don't know if Cycletron can import the scooters into Turkey as they promised. We don't need their services anymore if they fail to do the import. But this cannot be shown in the contract, because this contract need to be submitted to the authorities. I would say we can sign a 1 year contract to see how things go.{color}

